    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JNKDRQGM83HV3BQE3XZBR2MM\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to cancel a campaign that has been scheduled or partially sent. Campaigns that have already been fully sent cannot be cancelled. If you don't see the option to cancel a campaign by following the steps below, then sending is already complete and it can no longer be cancelled. </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>Learn how to <a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4411545074203\">make edits to a scheduled campaign</a>. </p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JNKDRQGMDF93RWKJWQ7W9AG5\">Cancel a scheduled campaign</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click on the <strong>Campaigns </strong>tab.</li>\n<li>Click the 3-dot icon to the right of the message you'd like to cancel. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Cancel</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716053599899\" alt=\"Option to cancel a campaign\" width=\"636\" height=\"252\">\n</li>\n<li>Confirm the cancellation in the modal that appears.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>After confirming your desire to cancel, you will see the status of the send change from <strong>Scheduled</strong> to <strong>Cancelled</strong><em>. </em>You will also see a message that indicates to resend, you will need to clone the cancelled campaign.</p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>For large campaigns, the scheduling process itself may take some time. A <strong>Cancel</strong> button will appear both while scheduling is still in progress, as well as after scheduling completes.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JNKDRQGNSBVC0KTVKR14CKY3\">Cancel a campaign mid-send</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click on the <strong>Campaigns </strong>tab.</li>\n<li>Click the 3-dots icon to the right of the message you'd like to cancel. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Cancel</strong>.</li>\n<li>Confirm the cancellation.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>After confirming your desire to cancel, you will see the status of the campaign change from <em>Sending</em> to <em>Cancelled During Send</em>.</p>\n<p>When you cancel a campaign mid-send, please note that Klaviyo cannot roll back (i.e., unsend) messages that have already been delivered. Cancelling only prevents any remaining messages (ones that are queued but not delivered) from sending.</p>\n<p>The number of messages from your campaign that ultimately get delivered depends on when you click cancel and how far along the sending process is. </p>\n<p>Available statistics for a campaign that is partially sent are available in the overview for that campaign. In this report, you can also see the date the campaign was scheduled and the cancellation date.</p>",
